WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:01.634
Trouble in paradise.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.636
Welcome to Unfiltered. I'm S.E. Cupp.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.505
What once seemed like

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.539
a Republican Party

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.841
united around

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.143
former President Donald Trump

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.612
now seems more like a house divided.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.680
And as Lincoln said,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.782
a house divided against itself

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.484
cannot stand.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.952
Since Trump announced his run

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.820
for president in 20, 24.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.989
You would have expected Trump World

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.125
to be completely re-energized

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.526
and coalesced

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.661
around their one time savior.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.730
But not so much.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.132
Steve Bannon, the former

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.434
architect of Trump's first campaign

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:37.737
and a chief strategist, hasn't been shy

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.006
about criticizing Trump's moves

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.274
since then.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.778
After Trump released a much mocked NFT,

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.380
Bannon took to his podcast to say,

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.549
I can't do this anymore.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.150
And called

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.218
for whoever was behind that decision

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.887
to be fired.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.622
I, for one, have to assume

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.524
Trump himself was behind that decision.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.360
And this week, Trump announced

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.461
he would appear with South

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.329
Carolina Senator Lindsey Graham

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.531
in that state

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.633
to reveal key campaign staff.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.035
Bannon did not take that news

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.837
well either, saying,

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.272
I have no earthly idea

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.740
why Graham's around

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.308
former President Trump.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.677
He's a cancer that's metastasizing

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.814
This follows another two key

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.649
supporters of Trump.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:24.451
The evangelical pastors, Franklin

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.119
Graham and Robert Jeffress,

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.387
both saying

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.822
they wouldn't endorse Trump

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:29.956
or any candidate

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:32.292
until after the primaries.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.294
Trump railed against that decision,

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.863
calling it a sign of disloyalty.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.898
And Trump's former press secretary,

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.733
the new governor of Arkansas,

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.435
Sarah Huckabee Sanders,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.704
has also refused to endorse him

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.707
right now for 20, 24

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.876
Now, the Republican on Republican crime

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:53.346
doesn't stop there, though hardly over.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:56.349
The RNC current chair, Ronna McDaniel

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.318
is in a bitter race against former

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.220
Trump lawyer Harmeet Dhillon

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.689
and Mypillow CEO Mike Lindell

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.758
to keep her position and the food fight

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.127
among these three

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.195
Republican Trump supporters

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.063
has not been pretty.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.432
Former Secretary of State

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.600
Mike Pompeo,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.635
also mulling a run for president,

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:19.105
has broken with Trump to defend more aid

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.140
to Ukraine

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.042
to defeat President Vladimir Putin there.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.613
Incidentally, Pompeo is also fighting

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:27.280
with former U.S.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.549
ambassador to the U.N., Nikki Haley.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:32.018
Another possible presidential candidate

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.453
over some comments

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.755
he made about her in his book.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.991
Over in the House, Representative

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.025
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.994
and Representative Matt Gaetz

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.263
are engaged in a petty fight over

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.397
who is the leading

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.533
MAGA voice in Congress.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:47.934
Now, lest

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.936
you think this is all bad news for Trump,

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.238
I actually have the opposite concern.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.407
With so many Republicans

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.676
contemplating a run in 20, 24.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.711
Pompeo. Haley. Mike Pence.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.047
Ron DeSantis. John Bolton.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.516
No one is poised to actually give him

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.218
a real challenge

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:05.852
He'll be a weaker

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.754
candidate than he was in 20, 16 and 20.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.355
20, for sure.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.157
But he only needs a plurality

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:13.126
to win the nomination.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:16.162
The infighting inside Trumpworld, RNC

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.764
and in the Republican House

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.966
will only be good for Trump

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.535
as he'll weaponize it to reward loyalty.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.070
This is

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:24.871
however, very bad

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.673
news for the Republican Party.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.575
Another two years of jockeying

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.476
for Trump's affection

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.312
and a likely Trump nomination

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.213
will continue

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.147
to do

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:36.583
what it has been for the past six years,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.085
weakening the GOP

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.487
to the point of utter uselessness.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.956
That's it for me. See you next week.

